<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I578a71907f3b209a0a494ce5fdfbbb86afe06dca" commit="cd48c1d098341d85e233b54f15349d073823e9b5" commit_message="crosh: added enrollment status crosh command  Added enterprise enrollment crosh command enroll_status [--mode] [--domain] [--user]  BUG=chromium:547310 TEST=ran cmd in test VM - enterprise enrolled and non enrolled  Change-Id: I578a71907f3b209a0a494ce5fdfbbb86afe06dca Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308661 Commit-Ready: Yehuda Yefet &lt;yyefet@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yehuda Yefet &lt;yyefet@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yehuda Yefet &lt;yyefetnyc@gmail.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Yehuda Yefet &lt;yyefet@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="308661" owner_email="yyefet@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/61/308661/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5e1f0dcc7879c394da254bc3a97df163cdf807ba" commit="c8b032f69d186f639d3933f5061a890fabf4da41" commit_message="Extract Weida from the generic touch updater  This CL removes the specialized logic for Weida touchscreens from the generic touch updater script, and moves it into it's own stand-alone script for Weida touch devices.  While this unfortunately will result in some duplicated code, it offers several advantages in the future:  1. We can edit the updater for one vendor without risking problems     with other vendors  2. The monolithic group-updater script grows ever more complex and     error prone as we add new vendors  3. This will offer us greater flexibility in the future as we add     support for additional touch devices -- they won't have to follow     the basic pattern of the others so closely.  BUG=chromium:525136 TEST=manually tested on Sumo, which is the only Weida device so far, and other device's seem to be uneffected  Change-Id: I5e1f0dcc7879c394da254bc3a97df163cdf807ba Signed-off-by: Charlie Mooney &lt;charliemooney@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/295869 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="295869" owner_email="charliemooney@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" ref="refs/changes/69/295869/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I17b46440819c459e61ac51a6de465c8e30fea0a5" commit="fee23d5469e06252c561ddbd5fe463294f322aa4" commit_message="fix tests broken for revised recovery process  This introduces BrokenScreenBypasser, a class derived from CtrlDBypasser, which can bypass the new 'broken' screen, and uses it to fix tests broken because of the revised recovery process.  BUG=chromium:501060,chrome-os-partner:46752 BRANCH=tot TEST=test_that -b veyron_jerry suite:faft_bios  Change-Id: I17b46440819c459e61ac51a6de465c8e30fea0a5 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308820 Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="308820" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/20/308820/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I74fd8d5344ffacad542cb442d4d122d2c4d80cf9" commit="6abbbe3792a5a91997e2949bcf22390625fbddea" commit_message="[autotest] Update ADBHost to use parent's collect_logs method.  There's no need to reimplement the collect_logs method since the inherited method calls the class get_file method which works just fine.  BUG=chromium:536120 TEST=Tried out the changes and it properly collected the dir of logs.  Change-Id: I74fd8d5344ffacad542cb442d4d122d2c4d80cf9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308951 Commit-Ready: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Paul Hobbs &lt;phobbs@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308951" owner_email="kevcheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/51/308951/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I95c79fe40d3ad79f37ce2eb586836e5de55be454" commit="c2be52b14360da365a605a55343aff2bd2b476a4" commit_message="libpayload: usbmsc: Add small delay during initialization to fix CZ60  We found that some SanDisk Cruizer Glide CZ60 sticks (confirmed on 16GB and 64GB versions) have a problem responding to our first GET_MAX_LUNS request right after they received their SET_CONFIGURATION. They will continually return a NAK until the host gives up (which is 2 user-noticable seconds for us). Adding a small delay of about 15us seems to be enough to fix the issue, but let's do 50 to be save.  Confirmed with both MT8173 and Intel LynxPoint XHCI controllers.  BRANCH=None BUG=chrome-os-partner:45473 TEST=No notable delay before detecting stick on Oak and Falco.  Change-Id: I95c79fe40d3ad79f37ce2eb586836e5de55be454 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308980 Reviewed-by: Patrick Georgi &lt;pgeorgi@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="308980" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/80/308980/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie44b416c9b196a429d6b257023316425a34e2583" commit="c834a4bb3b6458a93e44e6b4db51f602f8c3f61e" commit_message="cros_ec: Sync commands.h with current version in EC codebase  BUG=chromium:537269 TEST=None BRANCH=None  Change-Id: Ie44b416c9b196a429d6b257023316425a34e2583 Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/307884 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="307884" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/84/307884/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic963c82fea4ad10e8a5d7e476c5ce3e5ae525dad" commit="d4ff3dd55374bd9db19d14b62c0f7005b666194e" commit_message="charger: Add LIMIT_POWER charger param for low bat + weak charger  Add support for two new configs to specify critical energy battery percentage and critical external charger power. When we are under both thresholds, set the LIMIT_POWER charger parameter to inform the AP that it should conserve power to avoid brownout, and consider jumping to EC RW to negotiate PD.  In addition, modify the existing CONFIG_CHARGER_MIN_BAT_PCT_FOR_POWER_ON to allow power-up regardless of power level if a 15W+ charger is attached, since there is a reasonable chance it may speak PD and provide sufficient power to boot the AP.  BUG=chromium:537269 TEST=Manual on Glados. Set CHG_MW thresh to 20000, BAT_PCT to 50. Verify that LIMIT_POWER charger param is set until Zinger negotiates to 20V. Also veify that system can boot with Donette. BRANCH=None  Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: Ic963c82fea4ad10e8a5d7e476c5ce3e5ae525dad Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/306774 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alec Berg &lt;alecaberg@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="306774" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/74/306774/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifaad4570cb8e1c427e0c341073e4bacd29462974" commit="541ade8acb404e926984c281f0e5fb8d19fea944" commit_message="Remove cyan ec configuration  We no longer need to build cyan on ToT, so we can remove it.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44576 TEST=None BRANCH=None  Change-Id: Ifaad4570cb8e1c427e0c341073e4bacd29462974 Signed-off-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/309000 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="309000" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/00/309000/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5ab10bc3941e1f63d87c6fc2405e76869a6a4756" commit="0d44f8f51146bdc06604cde6875b13ee45662428" commit_message="cros_start_vm: Make it work with multiple USB devices.  This script is designed to work with multiple USB devices like e.g.   --usb_devices=18d1:4ee7,8087:09e  but it doesn't work without this change.  Change-Id: I5ab10bc3941e1f63d87c6fc2405e76869a6a4756 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/308906 Commit-Ready: David Zeuthen &lt;zeuthen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Zeuthen &lt;zeuthen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fa